From 9c624eded3d59d92fdaee9cdc58b539180574b75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jmosher <jmosher@mirantis.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:24:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] heat and placement: update liveness/readiness probes to use htk

heat and placement: update liveness/readiness probes to use healthcheck

Update liveness/readiness probes for heat-api, heat-cfn, and placement
to use the htk function.

Also updates heat-api, and heat-cfn to use /healthcheck endpoints for
readiness probe.  Leaves the liveness probe pointing at the uwsgi stats
port.

Signed-off-by: jmosher <jmosher@mirantis.com>
Change-Id: I0ec2713411c9c1ce984b0d0f8e18e5c1699c7db9

[Back-ported from OpenStack-Helm master branch]
The heat hunks of the upstream OpenStack-Helm change, which move
`heat-api` and `heat-cfn` readiness onto `/healthcheck`, have been
deliberately excluded as they are not required for the bug fix
that motivates this back porting.

This patch must be removed when the pinned openstack-helm revision is
advanced past the upstream change. The `liveness.port` override in
`placement-static-overrides.yaml` does not depend on this patch, as the
pre-existing inline template already honoured it; what this patch adds
is `params` support, so `timeoutSeconds` and `failureThreshold` are only
applied while it is in place. Both continue to work from the overrides
once the chart itself carries the upstream change.

Signed-off-by: Yathavan Parameshwaran <yathavan.parameshwaran@windriver.com>

[Updated to complete the back port]
The heat hunks excluded above are now included, so this is the
complete back port of the upstream change. They convert the `heat-api`
and `heat-cfn` probes to the htk function, add a `/healthcheck` route
served by `oslo_middleware` and point readiness at it, and leave
liveness on the uWSGI stats port as upstream does. They are required
so that the heat probe parameters can be set from
`heat-static-overrides.yaml`.

Signed-off-by: asyed1 <ahmed.syed@windriver.com>
